    <statement><p>Consider the functions given by <m>f(x) = 5-(x-1)^2</m> and <m>g(x) = 4-x</m>.</p>
<p><alert> (a) </alert> Use algebra to find the points where the graphs of <m>f</m> and <m>g</m> intersect. (If more than one point, use a comma to separate them.)</p>
<p>Point(s): <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> (b) </alert> Use <url href="">https://www.desmos.com/calculator</url> to accurately graph the functions <m>f(x)</m> and <m>g(x)</m>. Check to see if the points you found in part (a) are accurate.</p>
<p><alert> (c) </alert> Find and evaluate exactly an integral expression, <m>\int_a^b h(x)\ dx</m>, that represents the area between <m>y = f(x)</m> 
and the <m>x</m>-axis on the interval between the intersection points of <m>f</m> and <m>g</m>.</p>
